        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>reheapify</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::PriorityQueue::reheapify</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>reheapify - If an element in the queue has changed in a way that affects its standing in the comparison function, the queue&apos;s internal state becomes invalid. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Calling <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_priority_queue_1a79d40f085693726bbebb3a1d67303c01" kindref="member">reheapify()</ref> resets the queue&apos;s state, making it valid again. This operation has time complexity proportional to the number of elements in the queue, so don&apos;t plan to use it a lot. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
